      "id": "report",
      "kind": "api",
      "label": "GET /report",
      "sublabel": "INTERPRETED · plan + a status per step, from checkpoints",
      "note": "404s with \"no plan in this session\" until a plan event exists. That is correct — there is no report to give — and the panel now keeps its last good value instead of overwriting it with the 404.\n\nSince the supervisor writes checkpoints, the status here is observed rather than inferred. A third endpoint, GET /plan, adds what this one deliberately lacks: the CURSOR (next, blocked, revision), for a surface that renders controls rather than progress. See run-stepwise.",
      "frame": "serve",
      "tech": "Go net/http",
      "status": "done",
      "path": "internal/api/api.go",
