    {
      "ports": [],
      "tags": [],
      "id": "buildreport",
      "kind": "module",
      "label": "BuildReportAt",
      "sublabel": "decides done / partial / pending per step · checkpoints first",
      "note": "Status comes from checkpoint events, which the step supervisor now writes for every run — carrying the step INDEX, so a revision is distinguishable from a first attempt and two steps with the same name do not share a verdict.\n\nDisk reconciliation is a fallback again, for plans committed through the markdown path or before checks existed. It also no longer fires when steps SHARE a file set: a plan whose four steps all declared index.html used to flip every step to done the moment step 1 wrote it, Verify included (2026-09-04, car run).",
      "frame": "serve",
      "tech": "Go",
      "status": "done",
      "path": "internal/loop/report.go",
      "position": {
